<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Fire breaks out at Harties mine.</title>
<headline>Fire breaks out at Harties mine.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hartebeestfontein Gold Mining Company Ltd said on Tuesday a fire started at its No 6 shaft this morning and that 258 employees were evacuated.</p>
<p>The fire affected five stopes and one development area in a &quot;relatively&quot; low grade section of the mine. Eighty employees were referred to the Duff Scott Hospital for observation as a routine precaution, the mine said.</p>
<p>The mine which is in the Avgold Ltd stable was still attempting to put out the fire.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
